qtmultimedia 6.11.1 still calls CGWindowListCreateImage in the FFmpeg plugin's
window-capture code path. Apple obsoleted this API in macOS 15 and removed it
entirely from the SDK shipped with Xcode 26. Building against that SDK fails:

    qcgwindowcapture.mm:108:17: error: 'CGWindowListCreateImage' is unavailable:
        obsoleted in macOS 15.0 - Please use ScreenCaptureKit instead.

Apple's replacement (ScreenCaptureKit) hasn't been wired into qtmultimedia yet.
Guard the call with an SDK-version check and default-construct the imageRef to
null when building against SDK 15+. The existing `if (!imageRef)` branch below
turns that into a runtime CaptureFailed. GAV is a media player, not a screen
recorder, so window-capture-as-no-op is harmless here.

Verified against qtmultimedia v6.11.1.

--- a/src/plugins/multimedia/ffmpeg/darwin/qcgwindowcapture.mm
+++ b/src/plugins/multimedia/ffmpeg/darwin/qcgwindowcapture.mm
@@ -104,9 +104,15 @@
         if (auto rate = frameRateForWindow(m_wid))
             setFrameRate(*rate);

+#if defined(__MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MAX_ALLOWED) && __MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MAX_ALLOWED >= 150000
+        // CGWindowListCreateImage was removed in the macOS 15 SDK (Xcode 26). Stub to null;
+        // the null check below turns this into a runtime CaptureFailed error.
+        QCFType<CGImageRef> imageRef;
+#else
         QCFType<CGImageRef> imageRef =
                 CGWindowListCreateImage(CGRectNull, kCGWindowListOptionIncludingWindow, m_wid,
                                         kCGWindowImageBoundsIgnoreFraming);
+#endif
         if (!imageRef) {
             updateError(QPlatformSurfaceCapture::CaptureFailed,
                         QLatin1String("Cannot create image by window"));
